language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Seat six dinner guests around a round table so that as few neighbours as possible do not get along.
$ Guests: 0 Andrew, 1 Betty, 2 Cara, 3 Dave, 4 Erica, 5 Frank.
$ the compatible neighbour pairs, both orders (each guest sits next to only the guests listed for them)
letting Compatible = [[0,3],[0,5],[1,2],[1,4],[2,1],[2,5],[3,0],[3,4],[4,1],[4,3],[5,0],[5,2]]
$ x[k] is the guest in seat k, seats 1 to 6 going round the table
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..6)] of int(0..5)

branching on [x]
such that
$ each guest sits in exactly one seat
allDiff(x),
$ the guests in neighbouring seats get along, going round the table including the seat between the last and the first
$ (a 0-conflict seating exists for these guests, so zero conflicts is the minimum; the solver is asked for a conflict-free seating)
table([x[1], x[2]], Compatible),
table([x[2], x[3]], Compatible),
table([x[3], x[4]], Compatible),
table([x[4], x[5]], Compatible),
table([x[5], x[6]], Compatible),
table([x[6], x[1]], Compatible)
